Attribute VB_Name = "gfx_api_gl_c"
' lib/ivis_opengl/gfx_api_gl.cpp (and gfx_api_gl.h): gl_context, the OpenGL backend, ported whole
' but the Emscripten (WebGL) branches. There is one context, so gl_context is this module: its
' fields are the module's variables and its methods gl_context_<name>, called by
' gfx_api_context_vb's dispatch with the same parameters. Its textures, buffers and pipelines are
' the classes gl_texture, gl_texture_array, gl_gpurendered_texture, gl_buffer and
' gl_pipeline_state_object. The GL entry points are gl_win's (glad, generated by tools/gen_gl.py).
' C++'s delete is the last reference going (Set x = Nothing). The asserts that a size_t fits a
' GLint / GLsizei are left out (every size is a Long). The KHR_debug message callback also gets
' GL_DEBUG_OUTPUT_SYNCHRONOUS: a VB procedure cannot be called on a driver thread.
Option Explicit

Private Const GL_DEBUG_OUTPUT_SYNCHRONOUS As Long = &H8242&   ' (VB) see above

